  "id": "DrugBank_DB01240 - MONDO_5709",
  "verbalization": "Epoprostenol, a prostaglandin analog, is implicated in the treatment of allergic rhinitis through its anti-inflammatory properties. The evidence suggests that Epoprostenol may exert a therapeutic effect on the common cold by influencing the inflammatory cascade associated with allergic rhinitis. This is supported by its indication in allergic rhinitis, which in turn is linked to the common cold through a series of indirect pathways involving antihistamine and anti-inflammatory mechanisms. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Epoprostenol to allergic rhinitis and ultimately to the common cold indicates a potential role in modulating immune responses and reducing symptoms associated with the condition. The integrated evidence suggests that Epoprostenol may act through mechanisms that reduce inflammation and allergic reactions, potentially alleviating the symptoms of the common cold. However, the exact mechanism by which Epoprostenol influences the common cold remains to be fully elucidated, and further studies are needed to confirm its therapeutic potential in this context.",
